.TH SETLOCALE 3
.SH NAME
setlocale \- select a locale
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <locale.h>

char *
setlocale(category, locale)
int category;
char *locale;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
XENIX has a single locale, "C": the ASCII character set, and the
conventions of the C language for numbers and the like.
.B setlocale
returns "C" when
.I locale
is "C", the empty string, or NULL, and NULL, for a locale it does not
have, otherwise. The
.I category
is not looked at.
.PP
It is here for programs that call it.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
"C", or NULL.
.SH SEE ALSO
ctype(3)
.SH HISTORY
.B setlocale
is not in the C libraries of Version 7 AT&T UNIX, System V or 4.3BSD.
